us-east-1: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
-- want/negative_timeout.stderr --
dynaflux diff: -timeout -1m0s: want a duration above 0, such as 5m
Run 'dynaflux help diff' for usage.
-- want/negative_timeout.stdout --
-- want/newer_catalog_format.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-east-1: error DF7001: the deployed catalog has format 2; this dynaflux reads formats 1 to 1
  hint: upgrade dynaflux to the version that generated it, v9.0.0
-- want/newer_catalog_format.stdout --
us-east-1: catalog 0b0a51ca69f8, in format 2
us-west-2: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
-- want/not_deployed.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
-- want/not_deployed.stdout --
us-east-1: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
us-west-2: not deployed in shop-meta; everything is new
-- want/other_definitions.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-east-1, us-west-2: error DF7110: gone@v1 is deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2, and dynaflux.lock neither holds nor retires it; the deploy drops its table
  hint: restore its entry in dynaflux.lock; to drop the version, then retire it with dynaflux retire gone@v1
us-east-1, us-west-2: error DF7111: plan_counts@v1 has another definition in dynaflux.lock than deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2
  hint: dynaflux.lock and the deployed catalog disagree, as after a reverted lock or two branches deployed: restore dynaflux.lock from the deployed build, then run dynaflux generate
-- want/other_definitions.stdout --
us-east-1, us-west-2: catalog 02d426e4ece7, local ecccd95ebe0b
  view gone: current v1 → none
-- want/project_with_an_error.stderr --
dynaflux/bad.sql:1:14: error DF1101: expected a name, found ;
-- want/project_with_an_error.stdout --
-- want/queries_and_prune_window.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-east-1, us-west-2: warning DF7113: runtime.prune_window_seconds is 960, lower than the 1200 deployed
  hint: lower runtime.timeout_seconds in one deploy, and prune_window_seconds in a later one once the old timeout has passed (docs/spec/config.md)
-- want/queries_and_prune_window.stdout --
us-east-1, us-west-2: catalog 765e12650d5d, local ecccd95ebe0b
  query Legacy: removed
  query PageViews: changed
  query Plans: new
  runtime.prune_window_seconds: 1200 → 960
-- want/regions_apart.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
-- want/regions_apart.stdout --
us-east-1: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
us-west-2: catalog ba1292a27fc8, local ecccd95ebe0b
  query Plans: new
-- want/retired_in_a_region.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
us-west-2: error DF7114: dynaflux.lock keeps plan_counts@v1, which is retired in us-west-2
  hint: give the view a new version, by changing it or with dynaflux generate -rebuild plan_counts, then dynaflux retire plan_counts@v1
-- want/retired_in_a_region.stdout --
us-east-1, us-west-2: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
-- want/retiring_while_a_backfill_runs.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  region us-east-1
us-east-1: warning DF7112: page_counts@v2 becomes the current version of page_counts, but it is pending_backfill in us-east-1; its queries return ErrViewNotReady until it is live
  hint: deploy regional.yaml, run dynaflux backfill page_counts@v2 -region us-east-1 -prefix "", and deploy the application once it is live
us-east-1: error DF7115: dynaflux.lock retires page_seen@v1, which the deploy retires in us-east-1 without the checks of dynaflux retire, and its backfill is running
  hint: run dynaflux retire page_seen@v1 -prefix "" for this environment before the deploy
-- want/retiring_while_a_backfill_runs.stdout --
us-east-1: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, local 6a21b0f6cf13
  view page_counts: current v1 → v2
  view page_seen: current v1 → v2
  page_seen@v1: retired; the deploy deletes its table
  page_counts@v2: new; backfill it after the deploy
  page_seen@v2: new; backfill it after the deploy
-- want/same.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
-- want/same.stdout --
us-east-1, us-west-2: catalog ecccd95ebe0b, the same as the local one
-- want/streams.stderr --
store shop  prefix (none)  account 123456789012  regions us-east-1, us-west-2
dynaflux/shop.sql:9:1: error DF7104: stream page_views: PRIMARY KEY differs from the one deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2
  hint: keep it: a stream with another key is a new stream
dynaflux/shop.sql:4:5: error DF7102: stream page_views: column duration is UInt32, and UInt64 deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2
  hint: keep its type, and add a new column with the other one
dynaflux/shop.sql:5:5: error DF7103: stream page_views: the DEFAULT of column source differs from the one deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2
  hint: keep the deployed DEFAULT: the events stored before the column existed read as it
dynaflux/shop.sql:1:1: error DF7101: stream page_views: column referrer, deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2, was removed or renamed
  hint: put it back: a deployed stream only gains columns (docs/spec/sql.md §8.9)
dynaflux/shop.sql:7:5: error DF7105: stream page_views: new column country is neither Nullable nor has a DEFAULT, so the events deployed in us-east-1, us-west-2 have no value for it
  hint: make it Nullable, or give it a DEFAULT
us-west-2: warning DF7107: stream signups stops being archived with events: all; Firehose may drop one buffer, and the region's archive misses those events for good
  hint: keep archive.events: all in us-west-2, or accept the hole (docs/spec/infra.md §12)
us-east-1, us-west-2: warning DF7106: stream legacy is dropped; its table and archive stay
  hint: stop writing to it, and deploy once the projector's lag and the archive's freshness have drained (docs/spec/infra.md §12)
